<Layout title="Database">
    <section class="info">
        <h1> About Us</h1>
       <p>
         This website is a collaborative research initiative led by <a href="https://www.valeriosterzi.com/" target="_blank">
        Valerio Sterzi </a>(University of Bordeaux), offering independent insights and unaffiliated with the European Unified Patent Court (UPC). 
        Our goal is to deliver comprehensive data and visual insights on litigation cases at the UPC, with a particular focus on infringement actions filed since its opening on June 1, 2023. 
        Updated every two months, the data and figures presented here ensure that users have access to the most current information.
       </p>
       <p>
        This website uses the case information documents provided by the UPC on its website <a href="https://www.unified-patent-court.org/en/registry/presentation" target="_blank">
        https://www.unified-patent-court.org/en/registry/presentation </a>): we then clean up and consolidate the names of the parties, 
        and add additional information such as their country and economic sector and the characteristics of litigated patents. 
        A particular focus is placed on the role of Non-practicing Entities (NPEs) in these disputes and cases where standard essential patents (SEPs) are litigated.
       </p>

       <h1> Looking for data ? </h1>
       <h2> Are you researcher ? </h2>

       <p> 
        Data on litigation cases for the first year of UPC operations is available for research purposes. Please contact us (valerio.sterzi@u-bordeaux.fr) to obtain the full dataset. 
        You are free to use the data, provided that any paper or report published that uses these data includes the following literature citation:
       </p>
       <p> 
        Sterzi, V. (2024).  <a href=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13504851.2024.2426717 target="_blank">
        The European Unified Patent Court and non-practicing entities: a year of early evidence. </a>: a year of early evidence. Applied Economics Letters, 1–5. <a href=https://doi.org/10.1080/13504851.2024.2426717target="_blank">
        https://doi.org/10.1080/13504851.2024.2426717 </a>)
       </p>

       <p>
        If you encounter any errors or inaccuracies, please don’t hesitate to reach out—we appreciate your feedback to help us keep information accurate and reliable.
       </p>

        <h2> Are you non-researcher ? </h2>
        If you’re affiliated with a firm or another non-academic organization, please contact us (valerio.sterzi@u-bordeaux.fr) to discuss access options or potential collaborations.
        Among our collaborations, we are pleased to include the one with the industry coalition <a href=https://ip2innovate.eu/ target="_blank">
        IP2Innovate </a>: , whom we thank for their confidence.

        
</section>